From 374d02d720b53ef8ccc8e0dd259a7ee63709479f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:44:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] service: fix the leading whitespace test in
 valid_content_type()

isspace() returns any non-zero value for a space, not TRUE, so the test
never matched, and it was undefined for a negative char. A leading space
or tab was still rejected by the separator check below, so nothing
changes in practice; use g_ascii_isspace() so the test does what it
says.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/service.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/service.c b/src/service.c
index 8b2471b..eefc22d 100644
--- a/src/service.c
+++ b/src/service.c
@@ -918,7 +918,7 @@ valid_content_type (char *ct)
   if (strpbrk (ct, ctl_chars) != NULL)
     return FALSE;
 
-  if (isspace (*ct) == TRUE)
+  if (g_ascii_isspace (*ct))
     return FALSE;
 
   ct = strpbrk (ct, sep_chars);
-- 
